<Layout title="About me - Dylan Greene" description="A bit about Dylan Greene.">
  <h1 class="page-heading">About me</h1>

  <article>
    <p>
      I'm Dylan. I studied Software Engineering at the{" "}
      <a href="https://www.uottawa.ca">University of Ottawa</a> and came out with a
      BASc and a bad habit of taking things apart to see how they work.
    </p>
    <p>
      My career since then has been in government IT — full-stack work, a lot of AWS,
      and a fair amount of time spent on systems that were older than my degree.
      These days I'm at the{" "}
      <a href="https://www.cbsa-asfc.gc.ca">Canada Border Services Agency</a>,
      improving the applications people use to actually do their jobs.
    </p>
    <p>
      I've been involved at most points of the lifecycle, from early development
      through to deployment, and that's given me a real appreciation for the
      unglamorous parts. Anyone can build the happy path. The work is in everything
      that happens after it.
    </p>
    <p>
      Away from work I build small things that don't need to exist — a Discord bot, a
      browser extension whose only job is to show you a duck. A few of them end up on
      the <a href="/projects">projects</a> page.
    </p>
    <p>
      The fastest way to reach me is{" "}
      <a href="mailto:greenedy@hotmail.com">greenedy@hotmail.com</a>. I read
      everything.
    </p>
    <p>
      Best,
      <br />
      Dylan
    </p>
  </article>
</Layout>
